From: IYAKKI <noreply@iyakki.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/skl: do not lower the firmware's CDCLK while pipes are on

On Skylake, Kaby Lake and Coffee Lake (display version 9, not Broxton or
Gemini Lake) a CDCLK change can only be made with every pipe off. At the
first atomic commit after the boot-time hardware readout, i915 computes
the lowest CDCLK the current modes need and, when that is lower than the
clock the firmware left running, does a full modeset of every pipe just
to lower it ("Full modeset due to CDCLK change"). The screen the firmware
lit goes dark; on a Mac mini 2018 the on-board DP->HDMI converter then
stopped answering AUX during link training and the monitor lost the
signal for many seconds.

Keep the running CDCLK when it already satisfies the minimum and uses the
same VCO. Raising it still works as before; with no active pipes the
normal computation applies. Cost: CDCLK may stay higher than needed
while pipes are on (a little power).

Carried by IYAKKI for the optional Mac image variant only
(dist/buildroot/configs/iyakki_mac.fragment); not sent upstream.
Applies to Linux 6.12.112.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cdclk.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_cdclk.c
@@ -3070,6 +3070,21 @@
 
 	cdclk = skl_calc_cdclk(min_cdclk, vco);
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep a higher CDCLK that is already running (the firmware's, at the
+	 * first commit after the boot-time hardware readout) instead of
+	 * lowering it: on SKL/KBL/CFL a CDCLK change needs every pipe off, so
+	 * lowering it turns off the screen the firmware lit. Seen on a Mac mini
+	 * 2018 (Coffee Lake): "Full modeset due to CDCLK change" at i915 load,
+	 * after which its DP->HDMI converter failed link training. The clock
+	 * can still go up when a mode needs more; it only stops going down
+	 * while pipes are active, at the cost of a little power.
+	 */
+	if (cdclk_state->active_pipes && vco == cdclk_state->logical.vco &&
+	    cdclk_state->logical.cdclk > cdclk &&
+	    skl_calc_cdclk(cdclk_state->logical.cdclk, vco) == cdclk_state->logical.cdclk)
+		cdclk = cdclk_state->logical.cdclk;
+
 	cdclk_state->logical.vco = vco;
 	cdclk_state->logical.cdclk = cdclk;
 	cdclk_state->logical.voltage_level =
